  "full_text": "I just did the clothes and I made the mistake of putting all the clothes in one compartment. So I kind of got in trouble for putting too many jeans in one load with Dad's and these are cut-offs and so I said well they should fit now. So I put them all in one load. Then I realized I put my wallet in there and it gets worse. So then my parents had some papers from the mail because my dad sorts the mail on the washing machine. So earlier today I was like, oh, fuck it. And so I took the papers and I... Anyway, I sort of moved them so I didn't screw up totally. So then I come out here and I have to find my wallet because it's in the washing machine. So the question is, Terry, how fast are you and how good is your IQ? So I didn't find a wallet very quickly. It was completely soaked. And so then I put the wallet on the side and then I got the papers wet. So then I got my parents' papers wet. So it gets worse. anyway so uh um so now i got a wet wallet because i fell from fell from grace um so i was in here uh taking my video for diana and uh and i changed my routine and fell from grace and uh didn't record and stuff and anyway so uh so uh that was interesting falling from grace it's kind of like So you get further in life and then you realize what you fucked up. And the question is, do highs and lows balance? Yes. So is it inevitable? I don't know. What if doing grace is so... Grace itself must be a pain in the ass. Otherwise it wouldn't be worth anything. So, anyway.",
